The platform packages (@targeted-mutation/tmt-<os>-<cpu>) contain an
executable linked with the Lean 4 runtime and the libraries it bundles,
including GMP (LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later) and libuv (MIT).
Their licenses are in the lean/ directory of each platform package
(LICENSES from the Lean release, GPL-3.0.txt, libuv-LICENSE.txt and
libuv-LICENSE-extra.txt). To relink the executable against another GMP
build, replace lib/libgmp.a in that Lean toolchain and run
`npm run build:lean` in the source repository.
GMP is the version bundled by the Lean release named in
proof/lean/lean-toolchain; its source is available from https://gmplib.org/. The
proof sources and build scripts needed to relink that executable are in
the source repository under proof/lean and scripts/.
